<!--
  Container-side (dock) CycloneDDS config for the default --ethernet mode.
  Mounted into go2-sensors-humble at /config (read-only) via docker-compose.yml
  and used as the default CYCLONEDDS_URI (overridden only for --wifi, see
  tools/launch_all_sensors_docker.sh).

  MaxMessageSize is the critical setting here: CycloneDDS's own default
  (14720 B) is nearly 10x the real Ethernet MTU (1500 B). Left at default,
  large messages (RealSense raw color/depth images, the Hesai PandarXT-16's
  /rslidar_points PointCloud2) get sent as oversized UDP datagrams that the
  kernel then IP-fragments to fit the wire; fragile for reliable DDS
  delivery (losing any single 1500B fragment loses the whole multi-MB
  sample). Confirmed root cause (Sept 2026) of "RGB/depth show fine, LiDAR
  never shows in RViz" symptom: /proc/net/snmp on the PC showed a ~50% IP
  reassembly failure rate under load, and packet captures showed genuine
  ~13-14KB UDP payloads needing ~9-10 real IP fragments each. Capping
  MaxMessageSize (and FragmentSize, which controls DDSI-level sample
  chunking) safely under the 1500B MTU forces CycloneDDS to always emit
  single, unfragmented, MTU-safe UDP datagrams, eliminating IP
  fragmentation/reassembly entirely for this traffic. Verified fix:
  /rslidar_points went from 0 messages received (indefinitely) to a solid
  ~10Hz.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="0">
    <General>
      <Interfaces>
        <NetworkInterface name="eth0" />
      </Interfaces>
      <MaxMessageSize>1400B</MaxMessageSize>
      <FragmentSize>1300B</FragmentSize>
    </General>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
